main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ two-pack delegation: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A member constructor template with two parameter packs
(indices<Uf...>, Up... u), called from another constructor template's
mem-initializer delegation, fails deduction ("found no match for
symbol 'impl'") and the delegating constructor is left bodyless.  The
direct-call form recovers; the delegation does not.  Header-free
remaining layer of cpp11_tuple_leaf_no_body (libc++ __tuple_impl) and
the emplace family.  g++/clang++/valgrind clean.
